    Follow-up Level Views — account_payment_followup Module (PF-001)
    ================================================================

    List, form, search, and window action definitions for
    `account.followup.level` — the configuration model that defines
    escalation levels for overdue customer follow-ups.

    Implements:
      - PF-001: Follow-up level configuration (sequence, delay,
                action type, email template, triggers, minimum amount,
                multi-company scoping, archive toggle).

    External IDs defined (referenced by menuitem.xml and downstream
    modules in this module):
      - view_account_followup_level_list
      - view_account_followup_level_form
      - view_account_followup_level_search
      - action_account_followup_level   (referenced by
        `views/menuitem.xml` line 129 on `menu_account_followup_level`)

    Odoo 19.0 XML conventions:
      - `invisible` attribute (not `attrs`)
      - `column_invisible` for hidden list columns
      - `optional="hidden"` / `optional="show"` for toggleable columns
      - 4-space indentation
      - `widget="handle"` for drag-reorder on sequence
      - `widget="boolean_toggle"` for quick activate/archive on list
      - `widget="web_ribbon"` for archived state indicator on form
      - `widget="monetary"` with `options="{'currency_field': 'currency_id'}"`
        for min_amount; currency_id must be present (invisible) so the
        monetary widget can resolve the currency.

    Rules Compliance (AAP §0.7):
      - R-01: No cross-module imports — zero references to
              `account_asset_management`, `account_budget_management`,
              or `account_deferred_revenue` External IDs.
      - R-02: No Enterprise references — no `account_followup`,
              `account_reports`, `account_accountant` references.
      - R-03: Defines views for the NET-NEW model
              `account.followup.level` (no `inherit_id`).
      - R-05: N/A — does not touch `account.move` /
              `account.move.line` / `res.partner` fields.

    Model-Side Method Reference:
      The form's "Email Template" smart button calls
      `action_view_email_template`, which is defined on
      `account.followup.level` (see
      `models/account_followup_level.py` around line 674). The method
      opens the linked `mail.template` record in a form view; it
      returns `False` when no template is set, so the button itself is
      hidden (`invisible="not email_template_id"`) to avoid a no-op
      click.

    Access Control (per `security/ir.model.access.csv`):
      - account.group_account_user:    read-only (1,0,0,0)
      - account.group_account_manager: full      (1,1,1,1)
      Creation/editing of follow-up levels is restricted to accounting
      managers; all accountants can read configuration to understand
      the escalation workflow.

    Email Template Domain:
      The `email_template_id` Many2one uses
      `domain="[('model', '=', 'res.partner')]"` because
      `data/mail_template_data.xml` seeds all four default templates
      targeting `res.partner` (the follow-up cron iterates partners).
      Restricting the dropdown prevents users from selecting a template
      bound to a different model whose placeholders would fail to
      render.
-->
<odoo>
    <data>

        <!-- ============================================================ -->
        <!-- LIST (TREE) VIEW                                             -->
        <!-- ============================================================ -->
        <!--
            Primary list view used by the Configuration > Follow-up
            Levels menu. Sorted by (sequence, delay) so levels display
            in the order they fire. The `handle` widget on `sequence`
            enables drag-reorder; the `boolean_toggle` on `active`
            allows one-click archive/restore.

            Multi-company column is hidden by default and only visible
            to users with `base.group_multi_company`; single-company
            installations therefore see a clean four-column view.

            The `currency_id` field is required (as `column_invisible`)
            so the monetary widget on `min_amount` can resolve the
            currency symbol; the column itself is never rendered.
        -->
        <record id="view_account_followup_level_list" model="ir.ui.view">
            <field name="name">account.followup.level.list</field>
            <field name="model">account.followup.level</field>
            <field name="arch" type="xml">
                <list string="Follow-up Levels"
                      default_order="sequence, delay"
                      decoration-muted="not active">
                    <field name="sequence" widget="handle"/>
                    <field name="name"/>
                    <field name="delay"
                           string="Days After Due"/>
                    <field name="action_type"/>
                    <field name="email_template_id"
                           optional="show"/>
                    <field name="min_amount"
                           widget="monetary"
                           options="{'currency_field': 'currency_id'}"
                           optional="hidden"/>
                    <field name="currency_id"
                           column_invisible="True"/>
                    <field name="trigger_block_sales"
                           optional="hidden"/>
                    <field name="trigger_collection_list"
                           optional="hidden"/>
                    <field name="trigger_notify_sales_rep"
                           optional="hidden"/>
                    <field name="trigger_update_trust"
                           optional="hidden"/>
                    <field name="attach_invoices"
                           optional="hidden"/>
                    <field name="company_id"
                           groups="base.group_multi_company"
                           optional="hidden"/>
                    <field name="active"
                           widget="boolean_toggle"
                           optional="show"/>
                </list>
            </field>
        </record>

        <!-- ============================================================ -->
        <!-- FORM VIEW                                                    -->
        <!-- ============================================================ -->
        <!--
            Detail form for creating/editing a follow-up level.

            Structure:
              - Smart button bar: "Email Template" opens the linked
                mail.template form; hidden when no template is set.
              - Web ribbon: visual indicator when the level is archived
                (active == False).
              - Title: `name` placeholder "e.g. First Reminder".
              - Two-column group:
                  Left  — Basic Information (sequence, delay, description,
                          hidden active field for ribbon data binding).
                  Right — Action Configuration (action_type,
                          email_template_id, attach_invoices,
                          min_amount with monetary widget).
              - Notebook:
                  Page "Additional Actions" (trigger_*).
                  Page "Multi-Company" (company_id, visible only to
                                        users with multi-company group).

            Conditional visibility (Odoo 19 uses `invisible` attribute):
              * email_template_id — visible & required when
                action_type in ('automatic', 'email').
              * attach_invoices — visible when
                action_type in ('automatic', 'email'); silently
                ignored by the cron otherwise.
        -->
        <record id="view_account_followup_level_form" model="ir.ui.view">
            <field name="name">account.followup.level.form</field>
            <field name="model">account.followup.level</field>
            <field name="arch" type="xml">
                <form string="Follow-up Level">
                    <sheet>
                        <!-- Smart button bar.
                             The "Email Template" stat button calls the
                             model's `action_view_email_template`
                             method (models/account_followup_level.py
                             line 674) which returns an
                             `ir.actions.act_window` on the linked
                             mail.template. Hidden when no template is
                             configured to avoid a no-op click.
                        -->
                        <div name="button_box" class="oe_button_box">
                            <button name="action_view_email_template"
                                    type="object"
                                    class="oe_stat_button"
                                    icon="fa-envelope-o"
                                    invisible="not email_template_id">
                                <div class="o_stat_info">
                                    <span class="o_stat_text">Email</span>
                                    <span class="o_stat_text">Template</span>
                                </div>
                            </button>
                        </div>

                        <!-- Archive indicator ribbon. Visible when
                             active is False; the corresponding boolean
                             field is rendered invisible in the form
                             body so toggling must happen via the list
                             boolean_toggle or the Action > Archive
                             menu (driven by ir.actions.server).
                        -->
                        <widget name="web_ribbon"
                                title="Archived"
                                bg_color="bg-danger"
                                invisible="active"/>

                        <!-- Title block -->
                        <div class="oe_title">
                            <label for="name"/>
                            <h1>
                                <field name="name"
                                       placeholder="e.g. First Reminder"/>
                            </h1>
                        </div>

                        <!-- Primary configuration: two-column group -->
                        <group>
                            <group string="Basic Information"
                                   name="basic_info_group">
                                <field name="sequence"/>
                                <field name="delay"
                                       string="Days After Due Date"/>
                                <field name="description"
                                       placeholder="Internal description (visible to accountants only)"/>
                                <!-- `active` is rendered invisible: the
                                     web_ribbon above uses its value for
                                     display, while toggling is done from
                                     the list view or the chatter's Archive
                                     action. Keeping the field bound in
                                     the form preserves two-way data
                                     flow for the ribbon's reactive
                                     visibility expression.
                                -->
                                <field name="active" invisible="1"/>
                            </group>
                            <group string="Action Configuration"
                                   name="action_config_group">
                                <field name="action_type"/>
                                <field name="email_template_id"
                                       domain="[('model', '=', 'res.partner')]"
                                       invisible="action_type not in ('automatic', 'email')"
                                       required="action_type in ('automatic', 'email')"
                                       options="{'no_create': True}"/>
                                <field name="attach_invoices"
                                       invisible="action_type not in ('automatic', 'email')"/>
                                <field name="min_amount"
                                       widget="monetary"
                                       options="{'currency_field': 'currency_id'}"/>
                                <!-- `currency_id` must be present
                                     (invisible) in the form for the
                                     monetary widget on `min_amount` to
                                     render a currency symbol. It is
                                     computed from `company_id` on the
                                     model; users never edit it
                                     directly.
                                -->
                                <field name="currency_id" invisible="1"/>
                            </group>
                        </group>

                        <!-- Secondary configuration: notebook -->
                        <notebook>
                            <page name="triggers"
                                  string="Additional Actions">
                                <p class="text-muted">
                                    When this level fires, the following
                                    additional actions are executed on
                                    the partner (PF-001 Scenario 5).
                                    Each option is independent and may
                                    be combined with any
                                    <em>Action Type</em>.
                                </p>
                                <group>
                                    <group>
                                        <field name="trigger_block_sales"/>
                                        <field name="trigger_collection_list"/>
                                    </group>
                                    <group>
                                        <field name="trigger_notify_sales_rep"/>
                                        <field name="trigger_update_trust"/>
                                    </group>
                                </group>
                            </page>
                            <page name="multi_company"
                                  string="Multi-Company"
                                  groups="base.group_multi_company">
                                <group>
                                    <field name="company_id"
                                           options="{'no_create': True}"/>
                                </group>
                                <p class="text-muted">
                                    Follow-up levels are scoped per
                                    company. Users only see levels
                                    belonging to the companies they
                                    have access to. The
                                    <code>(sequence, company_id)</code>
                                    pair is unique — two levels in the
                                    same company cannot share the same
                                    sequence number.
                                </p>
                            </page>
                        </notebook>
                    </sheet>
                </form>
            </field>
        </record>

        <!-- ============================================================ -->
        <!-- SEARCH VIEW                                                  -->
        <!-- ============================================================ -->
        <!--
            Search view powering the Follow-up Levels list. The
            `active_levels` filter is applied by default via the window
            action context, so users initially see only active levels.

            Filter groupings (separated by `<separator/>` elements):
              1. Active / Archived status
              2. Action type filters (one per Selection value)
              3. Group By options (action type, company)
        -->
        <record id="view_account_followup_level_search" model="ir.ui.view">
            <field name="name">account.followup.level.search</field>
            <field name="model">account.followup.level</field>
            <field name="arch" type="xml">
                <search string="Follow-up Levels">
                    <!-- Autocomplete fields -->
                    <field name="name"/>
                    <field name="action_type"/>
                    <field name="email_template_id"/>

                    <separator/>

                    <!-- Active / Archived status -->
                    <filter name="active_levels"
                            string="Active"
                            domain="[('active', '=', True)]"/>
                    <filter name="archived"
                            string="Archived"
                            domain="[('active', '=', False)]"/>

                    <separator/>

                    <!-- Action type filters: one per Selection value -->
                    <filter name="automatic"
                            string="Automatic"
                            domain="[('action_type', '=', 'automatic')]"/>
                    <filter name="manual"
                            string="Manual"
                            domain="[('action_type', '=', 'manual')]"/>
                    <filter name="email_only"
                            string="Email Only"
                            domain="[('action_type', '=', 'email')]"/>
                    <filter name="letter_only"
                            string="Letter Only"
                            domain="[('action_type', '=', 'letter')]"/>
                    <filter name="phone_call"
                            string="Phone Call"
                            domain="[('action_type', '=', 'phone')]"/>
                    <filter name="legal"
                            string="Legal Action"
                            domain="[('action_type', '=', 'lawyer')]"/>

                    <!-- Group By options. The `<group>` element inside
                         a `<search>` view in Odoo 19 does not accept
                         `expand`/`string` attributes; collapsed-by-
                         default is the runtime default and the label
                         is rendered by the Group By menu itself.
                    -->
                    <group>
                        <filter name="group_action_type"
                                string="Action Type"
                                context="{'group_by': 'action_type'}"/>
                        <filter name="group_company"
                                string="Company"
                                context="{'group_by': 'company_id'}"
                                groups="base.group_multi_company"/>
                    </group>
                </search>
            </field>
        </record>

        <!-- ============================================================ -->
        <!-- WINDOW ACTION                                                -->
        <!-- ============================================================ -->
        <!--
            External ID `action_account_followup_level` is referenced
            by `views/menuitem.xml` (line 129) on the
            `menu_account_followup_level` menu item.

            Context:
              * search_default_active_levels: 1 — hides archived
                levels on initial load, matching the expectation that
                configuration users want to see live escalation rules.
        -->
        <record id="action_account_followup_level" model="ir.actions.act_window">
            <field name="name">Follow-up Levels</field>
            <field name="res_model">account.followup.level</field>
            <field name="view_mode">list,form</field>
            <field name="search_view_id" ref="view_account_followup_level_search"/>
            <field name="context">{'search_default_active_levels': 1}</field>
            <field name="help" type="html">
                <p class="o_view_nocontent_smiling_face">
                    Configure your first follow-up level
                </p>
                <p>
                    Follow-up levels define the escalation sequence for
                    customers who have overdue invoices. Each level
                    specifies how many days after the invoice due date
                    it triggers (<em>delay</em>), what action is
                    performed (<em>action type</em> — automatic email,
                    manual, phone call, letter, or legal action), and
                    which email template is used when the follow-up
                    cron fires.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Additional per-level options include attaching
                    invoice PDFs to reminder emails, blocking new sales
                    orders, adding the partner to a collection list,
                    notifying the salesperson, and updating the
                    partner's trust classification.
                </p>
                <p>
                    The (<em>sequence</em>, <em>company</em>) pair is
                    unique: two levels within the same company cannot
                    share the same sequence number.
                </p>
            </field>
        </record>

    </data>
</odoo>
